    "heading": "Cylinder [Area of Effect]",
    "lineStart": 13049,
    "lineEnd": 13053
  },
  "section": "8.44",
  "rulesText": "A Cylinder is an area of effect that extends in straight lines from a point of origin located at the center of the circular top or bottom of the Cylinder. The effect that creates a Cylinder specifies the radius of the Cylinder's base and the Cylinder's height.\n\nA Cylinder's point of origin is included in the area of effect."
}
